From 472e0bb08707cdc27bbc32b3193eea7de0456c32 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:42:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm: drm_dvbridge.h, one header for the policy of the Dolby
 Vision tunnel

i915 (intel_dv_lab_policy.h), amdgpu (amdgpu_dm_dvbridge.h) and the
Low-Latency header (drm_dvbridge_ll.h) each had their own copy of the walk
of the Dolby VSVDB rule, i915 a second copy for the reason of the log, the
Low-Latency header two more, and i915 and amdgpu their own table of the
CTA VICs of the tunnel and their own lines for its AVI InfoFrame and Dolby
VSIF. A host test kept the copies equal; a change of the rule had to be
made five times.

include/drm/drm_dvbridge.h has the rule once: drm_dvbridge_edid_read()
walks the EDID one time and says what it found (the first test that
refuses, in the order of the walk, or the Dolby block taken, with what it
advertises: Standard, Low-Latency, 2160p60); drm_dvbridge_sink_why() names
it for the kernel log, for Standard or for Low-Latency; and
drm_dvbridge_avi_vic(), drm_dvbridge_tunnel_avi() and
drm_dvbridge_tunnel_vsif() are the VIC table, the AVI fields and the Dolby
VSIF of the tunnel. intel_dv_lab_edid(), intel_dv_lab_edid_why(),
amdgpu_dm_dvbridge_edid_standard(), drm_dvbridge_ll_edid() and
drm_dvbridge_ll_edid_why() stay as one-line names of it (the host test of
the rule calls them). amdgpu reads the sink of the stream once in
amdgpu_dm_dvbridge_fill_stream() and in its refusal.

Nothing changes in what is decided or sent: *p60 is left as the walk had
it when it stopped, as before, and the AVI fields are the same ones in
the same drivers (the YQ field stays as each driver sets it for RGB). The
verdicts of the five functions and the VIC table, printed for the 603
real EDIDs of the host test, the Amlogic presets and 400 mutations of
each (242061 lines), are byte for byte those of the tree before. The
policy test, the three-way test with Kodi (2226560 EDIDs) and the corpus
test pass; their 50 mutations, rewritten for the new places of the rule,
are all caught. W=1 on i915, its xe copies and amdgpu_dm: no warning.
